# Allowlist, not a denylist: same rationale as leaf/.gitignore.
#
# On a machine where ~/.config/vicinae or ~/.local/share/vicinae does not exist
# yet, stow tree-folds it into this directory, and everything Vicinae writes at
# runtime (settings.json, its sqlite databases, the clipboard store) would land
# here. Ignore the lot, re-include only what the repo declares.
.config/vicinae/*
!.config/vicinae/dotfiles.jsonc
.local/share/vicinae/*
!.local/share/vicinae/scripts/
